A new continuously recurrent Qwen3.5-0.8B decoder gave *32/96 operationally correct responses versus 14/96* for untouched Base in *134.93 versus 824.89 seconds*. On human-authored questions over real tables it executed the required lookup and gave the answer on *7/32 versus 2/32*. All seven loop answers matched the source cell exactly. On WinoGrande it answered *23/48 versus 11/48* sentences correctly, but repeated the identical visible answer across 22 of 24 opposite-meaning pairs. Each model solved just *1/24* complete meaning pairs. Each missed all eight complete two-request package conversations. The loop reached its first token slightly later in aggregate, 11.95 versus 11.69 seconds. The primary gain was two complete meaning-or-table pairs versus one, with no significant paired difference. The adapter is reproducible and opt-in. General reasoning superiority and a default replacement remain unestablished.
